- The rule of law fosters public trust, confidence and social stability.
- The rule of law supports economic development through legal certainty.
- Businesses and investors rely on rule of law for property right protection.
- A written constitution alone does not guarantee genuine rule of law in practice.
- Political culture and enforcement matter as much as formal legal text.
- Arbitrary arrest and detention violate the principle of the rule of law.
- Retroactive laws that punish past conduct undermine the rule of law.
- Corruption and impunity for officials undermine the rule of law.
- The rule of law is closely linked to the doctrine of separation of powers.
- Judicial review helps enforce the rule of law against unconstitutional actions.
